<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" ?><transcript><text start="0.719" dur="5.12">Hello everybody.</text><text start="2.639" dur="4.881">I&amp;#39;m going to take a nice trip to Kansas</text><text start="5.839" dur="4.241">where we have a wonderful Senator</text><text start="7.52" dur="5.28">Marshall. He&amp;#39;s going to do very well. I</text><text start="10.08" dur="5.759">think he&amp;#39;s going to uh win. I won the</text><text start="12.8" dur="4.88">state by many, many points. I love the</text><text start="15.839" dur="5.44">people of Kansas and that&amp;#39;s why I go</text><text start="17.68" dur="6.32">there. So hopefully uh we&amp;#39;ll have a a</text><text start="21.279" dur="4.16">great victory in Kansas, but we&amp;#39;ll know</text><text start="24" dur="3.84">soon enough. I think he&amp;#39;s going to do</text><text start="25.439" dur="5.441">very well. Roger Marshall is one of the</text><text start="27.84" dur="3.199">finest people in in government as far as</text><text start="30.88" dur="3.159">I&amp;#39;m</text><text start="31.039" dur="3">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; concerned.</text><text start="35.2" dur="4.4">You said that you don&amp;#39;t want to drive</text><text start="37.04" dur="4.56">the Vladimir Putin away from the bar.</text><text start="39.6" dur="3.36">What guarantee has he made you that he&amp;#39;s</text><text start="41.6" dur="3.119">willing to strike a bargain?</text><text start="42.96" dur="4.64">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; Well, you&amp;#39;ll see soon enough because I&amp;#39;m</text><text start="44.719" dur="6.081">trying to get a hostage that uh the</text><text start="47.6" dur="5.92">country&amp;#39;s been after for a long time and</text><text start="50.8" dur="5.68">before my time and let&amp;#39;s see what</text><text start="53.52" dur="4.96">happens. That&amp;#39;ll be that&amp;#39;ll be soon. We</text><text start="56.48" dur="4.96">also have a very good situation with</text><text start="58.48" dur="5.28">respect to Iran. He&amp;#39;s laying off Iran.</text><text start="61.44" dur="4.719">It&amp;#39;s nice because we&amp;#39;re hitting Iran</text><text start="63.76" dur="5.44">very hard as you know economically as</text><text start="66.159" dur="6">well as militarily and Russia&amp;#39;s done</text><text start="69.2" dur="5.76">nothing there that we can see and I</text><text start="72.159" dur="4.64">think uh that&amp;#39;s a very positive and of</text><text start="74.96" dur="5.12">course we&amp;#39;re negotiating with him on</text><text start="76.799" dur="5.36">Ukraine. So uh I&amp;#39;m not looking to break</text><text start="80.08" dur="4.079">up negotiations right in the middle. And</text><text start="82.159" dur="4.881">by the way, I have the right to do that</text><text start="84.159" dur="4.64">at any time immediately. So if things</text><text start="87.04" dur="4.56">don&amp;#39;t work out, I can always do it.</text><text start="88.799" dur="5.041">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; Have you ever Republicans who have been</text><text start="91.6" dur="5.44">speaking out? Have you seen the</text><text start="93.84" dur="4.639">Republicans who have been speaking out?</text><text start="97.04" dur="5.28">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; Well, I think when they find out what</text><text start="98.479" dur="6">the deal is, they uh when I&amp;#39;ve had four</text><text start="102.32" dur="4.64">of them call up and they only put out</text><text start="104.479" dur="4.481">word last night. I&amp;#39;m in the midst of</text><text start="106.96" dur="4">negotiating a deal. When you&amp;#39;re</text><text start="108.96" dur="4.08">negotiating a deal, you don&amp;#39;t do that to</text><text start="110.96" dur="4.24">the people you&amp;#39;re negotiating and the</text><text start="113.04" dur="4">deals Ukraine deal. Also, I&amp;#39;m</text><text start="115.2" dur="4.4">negotiating with them on Iran because</text><text start="117.04" dur="4.399">they&amp;#39;ve been very well behaved on Iran.</text><text start="119.6" dur="4.559">Also, I&amp;#39;m negotiating with them on</text><text start="121.439" dur="6.88">hostages and I&amp;#39;m also negotiating on</text><text start="124.159" dur="5.761">diesel. So, when you when you</text><text start="128.319" dur="3.681">when you&amp;#39;re negotiating, you don&amp;#39;t do</text><text start="129.92" dur="3.92">that. When I tell that to Republicans</text><text start="132" dur="4.16">that speak out and there aren&amp;#39;t many of</text><text start="133.84" dur="4">them uh because they have confidence in</text><text start="136.16" dur="3.68">him, I&amp;#39;m the one that got them there.</text><text start="137.84" dur="3.759">I&amp;#39;m the one that&amp;#39;s winning. I&amp;#39;m the one</text><text start="139.84" dur="4.24">that&amp;#39;s doing the rallies. It&amp;#39;s taking</text><text start="141.599" dur="4.401">people into a winning position. When you</text><text start="144.08" dur="3.44">look at what&amp;#39;s happened, if you take a</text><text start="146" dur="4.959">look at what&amp;#39;s happened since I&amp;#39;ve been</text><text start="147.52" dur="6.079">doing these massive, totally sold out</text><text start="150.959" dur="5.201">rallies, nobody&amp;#39;s ever seen anything</text><text start="153.599" dur="5.28">like it. As an example, we&amp;#39;re up in</text><text start="156.16" dur="5.04">Texas. We weren&amp;#39;t We&amp;#39;re up in Alaska. We</text><text start="158.879" dur="4.801">weren&amp;#39;t. We&amp;#39;re up everybody every place</text><text start="161.2" dur="3.6">that I&amp;#39;ve gone to. We&amp;#39;re up. Mr.</text><text start="163.68" dur="3.68">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; President, have you agreed to a</text><text start="164.8" dur="3.36">trilateral meeting with President</text><text start="167.36" dur="3.36">talk about.</text><text start="168.16" dur="5.2">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; No, but I would I would do it. Not so</text><text start="170.72" dur="5.2">much for Ukraine. I because Russia</text><text start="173.36" dur="4.56">frankly has been fine on Ukraine. They</text><text start="175.92" dur="4.24">haven&amp;#39;t been doing much. And the same</text><text start="177.92" dur="3.92">thing with China. We would have it to</text><text start="180.16" dur="3.28">talk about nuclear weapons and</text><text start="181.84" dur="3.44">denuclearization.</text><text start="183.44" dur="3.439">And anytime I can have a meeting on</text><text start="185.28" dur="4.239">denuclearization.</text><text start="186.879" dur="4.561">So we have more during my term I did it.</text><text start="189.519" dur="4.8">We have more nuclear weapons than</text><text start="191.44" dur="5.519">anybody. Russia is second. China&amp;#39;s third</text><text start="194.319" dur="4.321">but catching up. China was way behind</text><text start="196.959" dur="4.881">and now they&amp;#39;re catching up. It&amp;#39;ll take</text><text start="198.64" dur="4.959">them about probably five years. We would</text><text start="201.84" dur="3.28">schedule a meeting based on the</text><text start="203.599" dur="3.601">denuclearization</text><text start="205.12" dur="4.96">and that&amp;#39;s a very positive thing for the</text><text start="207.2" dur="5.119">world. So, I would do it if if they want</text><text start="210.08" dur="4.239">to have a I just heard about it. If</text><text start="212.319" dur="4.721">they&amp;#39;d like to have it, I think it would</text><text start="214.319" dur="4.56">be held in China. He just left here. Uh</text><text start="217.04" dur="3.279">if President Xi wants to have it, I&amp;#39;d</text><text start="218.879" dur="4.561">have it. I&amp;#39;m sure we&amp;#39;re talking about</text><text start="220.319" dur="4.56">other things like trade, too, but um</text><text start="223.44" dur="3.76">yeah, I would do that. Have you</text><text start="224.879" dur="4.161">investigated at all who slowed down or</text><text start="227.2" dur="3.52">specifically the interruption of</text><text start="229.04" dur="2.16">Starling Ukraine who ordered that</text><text start="230.72" dur="2.239">interruption?</text><text start="231.2" dur="4.92">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; I don&amp;#39;t know who it was, but I&amp;#39;d like to</text><text start="232.959" dur="3.161">find out</text><text start="236.48" dur="4.399">MacBron is blaming the Iran war and you</text><text start="238.799" dur="2.401">essentially for the rioting in France</text><text start="240.879" dur="3.36">right now.</text><text start="241.2" dur="5.28">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; I don&amp;#39;t think I think that Who you with?</text><text start="244.239" dur="5.441">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; No, sir. Mary Daily Wire.</text><text start="246.48" dur="4.959">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; Oh, Daily Wire&amp;#39;s good. Sorry. Daily Mr.</text><text start="249.68" dur="2.32">President, would you do a meeting with</text><text start="251.439" dur="3.52">President</text><text start="252" dur="4.959">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; Emanuel? He&amp;#39;s a friend of mine. I told</text><text start="254.959" dur="4.161">him a long time ago, you&amp;#39;re making a big</text><text start="256.959" dur="4.321">mistake in France. You&amp;#39;re letting</text><text start="259.12" dur="4.72">everybody from the world come in. The</text><text start="261.28" dur="4.08">whole world was coming in. And you know,</text><text start="263.84" dur="4">as you know, Paris is going to be a</text><text start="265.36" dur="5.2">Muslim city very soon. And that wasn&amp;#39;t</text><text start="267.84" dur="4.639">the deal. That wasn&amp;#39;t the deal. I told</text><text start="270.56" dur="4">Emanuel, you should close up your</text><text start="272.479" dur="4.72">borders. And let&amp;#39;s see. I&amp;#39;ve known him</text><text start="274.56" dur="4.48">for probably eight or nine years. I told</text><text start="277.199" dur="4.241">him as soon as I met him, I said,</text><text start="279.04" dur="4.24">&amp;quot;You&amp;#39;re making a big mistake. We closed</text><text start="281.44" dur="3.68">our borders.&amp;quot; He did.</text><text start="283.28" dur="3.84">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; And you know what? His borders are a</text><text start="285.12" dur="3.68">problem. And he also has a little bit of</text><text start="287.12" dur="3.28">a problem with energy, but they have</text><text start="288.8" dur="4">gone. You know, they&amp;#39;re doing better</text><text start="290.4" dur="4.32">than others. But Emanuel should have</text><text start="292.8" dur="2.959">closed his borders a long time ago. I</text><text start="294.72" dur="3.36">told him to do.</text><text start="295.759" dur="4.321">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; Mr. President</text><text start="298.08" dur="4.48">says you&amp;#39;re supporting Putin by waving</text><text start="300.08" dur="5.679">these sanctions. No, I&amp;#39;m I&amp;#39;m supporting</text><text start="302.56" dur="3.84">uh stopping the war between Russia and</text><text start="305.759" dur="1.681">Ukraine.</text><text start="306.4" dur="3.04">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; How does God help?</text><text start="307.44" dur="5.199">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; And you know what? Why? Because that&amp;#39;s</text><text start="309.44" dur="5.52">what I do for a living. And frankly, uh</text><text start="312.639" dur="4.4">Zilinski is not helping matters much. I</text><text start="314.96" dur="4.72">think he doesn&amp;#39;t want to stop it. But I</text><text start="317.039" dur="7.041">want to see people not die. They&amp;#39;re</text><text start="319.68" dur="7.04">losing probably on average 25 to 35,000</text><text start="324.08" dur="4.959">soldiers every single month. All I want</text><text start="326.72" dur="4.88">to do, I don&amp;#39;t care. I want to get the</text><text start="329.039" dur="4.081">war stopped. I don&amp;#39;t want to see 25</text><text start="331.6" dur="4.319">35,000.</text><text start="333.12" dur="6.32">Last month it was 32,000. I don&amp;#39;t want</text><text start="335.919" dur="5.361">to see 32,000 soldiers dead. Has nothing</text><text start="339.44" dur="4.88">to do with this country. But you know</text><text start="341.28" dur="5.759">what? I from a human standpoint. Ukraine</text><text start="344.32" dur="5.12">is losing a lot of Ukraine is losing all</text><text start="347.039" dur="4.961">of its men. You know, I was watching a</text><text start="349.44" dur="4.88">woman on television the other night and</text><text start="352" dur="4.8">she blames a little. She said he&amp;#39;s</text><text start="354.32" dur="4.879">killing our men. And the fact is, she</text><text start="356.8" dur="5.28">said, and it was very poignant. She</text><text start="359.199" dur="5.601">said, &amp;quot;Our men are dying. Our men have</text><text start="362.08" dur="5.04">no legs in many cases. You look around,</text><text start="364.8" dur="4.48">they have no legs. They&amp;#39;re in mental</text><text start="367.12" dur="4.56">institutions.&amp;quot; She&amp;#39;s talking about</text><text start="369.28" dur="4.4">Ukraine. And she&amp;#39;s very well known. And</text><text start="371.68" dur="4.48">they want to put her in prison. I want</text><text start="373.68" dur="6.079">to see the war stop. You&amp;#39;re losing</text><text start="376.16" dur="7.12">tremendous numbers of mostly young</text><text start="379.759" dur="7.121">military men. And that means 25,000 to</text><text start="383.28" dur="7.039">35,000 a month. All I want is for Russia</text><text start="386.88" dur="5.12">and Ukraine to stop that stupid war. Mr.</text><text start="390.319" dur="4.88">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; President, would you meet with President</text><text start="392" dur="4.72">Xia and and discuss the end of the war</text><text start="395.199" dur="3.681">without Yolinski there?</text><text start="396.72" dur="3.68">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; Well, I would meet in order anything I</text><text start="398.88" dur="3.759">can do to end the war, whether</text><text start="400.4" dur="4.96">somebody&amp;#39;s there or not. Whatever I can</text><text start="402.639" dur="4.641">do to end the war and they do want to</text><text start="405.36" dur="3.92">have a meeting at my suggestion because</text><text start="407.28" dur="5.039">I&amp;#39;m going to be over in China in</text><text start="409.28" dur="5.52">November on the denuclearization.</text><text start="412.319" dur="4.961">And if we could do denuclearization, I</text><text start="414.8" dur="4.799">will have done the world a big big</text><text start="417.28" dur="4.479">favor. But you said the wrong side of</text><text start="419.599" dur="3.04">history here. Sir, you&amp;#39;re on the wrong</text><text start="421.759" dur="1.521">side of history.</text><text start="422.639" dur="2.241">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; What&amp;#39; you say?</text><text start="423.28" dur="3.6">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; Silinski says you&amp;#39;re on the wrong side</text><text start="424.88" dur="2.879">of history on this one.</text><text start="426.88" dur="1.439">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; Silinski said</text><text start="427.759" dur="2.321">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; yes.</text><text start="428.319" dur="4.401">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; Silinski doesn&amp;#39;t know what he&amp;#39;s talking</text><text start="430.08" dur="4.48">about. Silinski is a man that should</text><text start="432.72" dur="3.919">have had this war settled a long time</text><text start="434.56" dur="3.759">ago. If he would have listened to me, he</text><text start="436.639" dur="3.601">would have made a much better deal a</text><text start="438.319" dur="4.16">long time ago and he&amp;#39;d have a million</text><text start="440.24" dur="3.44">people living from his side. Mr.</text><text start="442.479" dur="3.041">President,</text><text start="443.68" dur="4.4">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; and to be honest, I don&amp;#39;t think I think</text><text start="445.52" dur="4.88">it&amp;#39;s time for somebody else to negotiate</text><text start="448.08" dur="5.92">on behalf of Ukraine because what&amp;#39;s</text><text start="450.4" dur="5.68">happened, very little land is, but a</text><text start="454" dur="4.16">million people, a tremendous number of</text><text start="456.08" dur="4.64">people are dead. They&amp;#39;re losing their</text><text start="458.16" dur="4.64">male population. Ukraine could have had</text><text start="460.72" dur="4">this thing settled a long time ago if</text><text start="462.8" dur="3.839">you would have listened to me. And you</text><text start="464.72" dur="4.56">remember the Oval Office, he would have</text><text start="466.639" dur="4.721">had this settled a long time ago. Maybe</text><text start="469.28" dur="3.919">it&amp;#39;s time for Zilinski to get somebody</text><text start="471.36" dur="5.6">else to negotiate.</text><text start="473.199" dur="5.44">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; Is it a bad sign for a bad</text><text start="476.96" dur="3.76">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; Is it a bad sign for Republicans that</text><text start="478.639" dur="3.84">you have to go campaign in Kansas today?</text><text start="480.72" dur="4.56">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; No. I tell you, I have a man named</text><text start="482.479" dur="5.761">Roger, and you know him very well. Roger</text><text start="485.28" dur="5.759">Marshall. He&amp;#39;s a fantastic senator. He&amp;#39;s</text><text start="488.24" dur="4.48">one of the best. It&amp;#39;s a close race. It</text><text start="491.039" dur="4.641">shouldn&amp;#39;t be. As you know, I won by a</text><text start="492.72" dur="5.919">tremendous amount, like 25, 30 points. I</text><text start="495.68" dur="5.84">won by a lot. Kansas, and they should be</text><text start="498.639" dur="4.56">winning by a lot. So, uh, I went to</text><text start="501.52" dur="2.32">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; first. You want to listen to him?</text><text start="503.199" dur="4.4">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; Yes, sir.</text><text start="503.84" dur="8.8">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; I went to Alaska and Dan Sullivan is up.</text><text start="507.599" dur="8.721">I went to Ohio, John is up. I went to</text><text start="512.64" dur="8.44">Texas and Ken Paxton is up so far. And I</text><text start="516.32" dur="4.76">went to many other places, wherever.</text><text start="521.36" dur="5.28">Wherever I go, they seem to be up and I</text><text start="524.64" dur="5.199">have the biggest rallies anybody&amp;#39;s ever</text><text start="526.64" dur="5.92">seen. Uh they&amp;#39;re packed houses. We have</text><text start="529.839" dur="4.56">thousands and thousands of people today</text><text start="532.56" dur="4.719">and beyond the house. They&amp;#39;re broadcast</text><text start="534.399" dur="5.201">all over. And my rallies are having a</text><text start="537.279" dur="4.961">huge impact and a positive impact on the</text><text start="539.6" dur="6.08">Republican party. I&amp;#39;m going to Kansas</text><text start="542.24" dur="5.52">because I want it by a lot. and the</text><text start="545.68" dur="4.159">great senator and he&amp;#39;s a great senator.</text><text start="547.76" dur="6.48">Roger Marshall, he&amp;#39;s one of the best</text><text start="549.839" dur="6.161">senators. He&amp;#39;s um I think he&amp;#39;s tied or</text><text start="554.24" dur="3.76">up by a little bit according to polls.</text><text start="556" dur="4.16">Look, the polls are fake. But according</text><text start="558" dur="4.72">to polls, so I want to make sure Roger</text><text start="560.16" dur="5.28">Marshall gets it. Roger Marshall is a</text><text start="562.72" dur="4.16">great man and he&amp;#39;s a great senator. So</text><text start="565.44" dur="1.68">that&amp;#39;s why I&amp;#39;m going. I think that&amp;#39;s</text><text start="566.88" dur="2.639">fine.</text><text start="567.12" dur="5.12">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; Why do you think it&amp;#39;s so</text><text start="569.519" dur="6.281">good?</text><text start="572.24" dur="3.56">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; Yeah, we share.</text><text start="576.959" dur="2.801">We appreciate a lot. We&amp;#39;ve given a lot</text><text start="578.56" dur="2.8">to Ukraine.</text><text start="579.76" dur="4.56">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; You know what? We&amp;#39;ve given a lot to</text><text start="581.36" dur="5.76">Ukraine. They&amp;#39;ve given nothing to us.</text><text start="584.32" dur="6.079">Remember that. We&amp;#39;ve given hundreds of</text><text start="587.12" dur="5.04">billions of dollars. I gave the Javelins</text><text start="590.399" dur="5.041">to Ukraine when he knocked out. That was</text><text start="592.16" dur="5.44">me. Obama gave him pillows. You know the</text><text start="595.44" dur="4.72">expression, Obama gave him sheets and</text><text start="597.6" dur="4.88">pillows. Trump gave him the jab. So</text><text start="600.16" dur="4.64">don&amp;#39;t tell me about Ukraine. We&amp;#39;ve given</text><text start="602.48" dur="2.96">a lot to Ukraine. They&amp;#39;ve given us</text><text start="604.8" dur="2.8">nothing.</text><text start="605.44" dur="4.48">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; Republicans are saying you&amp;#39;re going to</text><text start="607.6" dur="5.04">put money in Mr.</text><text start="609.92" dur="4.72">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; Russia could have done way more to help.</text><text start="612.64" dur="5.199">You said Russia could have done way more</text><text start="614.64" dur="5.28">to help Iran if they wanted. Russia</text><text start="617.839" dur="3.761">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; Russia could have done a lot more.</text><text start="619.92" dur="4.4">That&amp;#39;s right. Russia could have done a</text><text start="621.6" dur="4.799">lot more to help if you could put it</text><text start="624.32" dur="4.079">bluntly. Russia could have done a lot</text><text start="626.399" dur="4.801">more to help Iran. Russia&amp;#39;s done very</text><text start="628.399" dur="4.721">little for Iran. China could have done a</text><text start="631.2" dur="4.72">lot more for him. They&amp;#39;ve done and I</text><text start="633.12" dur="6.08">remember that when China does not that</text><text start="635.92" dur="5.359">much, maybe nothing almost, but very</text><text start="639.2" dur="5.52">little for 