ed deal</text><text start="707.2" dur="4.16">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; because up until then for years, she was</text><text start="709.76" dur="4.639">always calling me correctly. I was going</text><text start="711.36" dur="5.44">to win by a lot. I had a great win in</text><text start="714.399" dur="5.201">Iowa and she said I was going to lose by</text><text start="716.8" dur="6.12">four and I won by almost 20. That was a</text><text start="719.6" dur="3.32">crooked deal.</text><text start="724.079" dur="4.161">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; On the French proess on the French</text><text start="726.399" dur="3.281">process, what&amp;#39;s your message to you the</text><text start="728.24" dur="3.68">young people in France who are</text><text start="729.68" dur="4.159">protesting kids?</text><text start="731.92" dur="4.479">&amp;gt;&amp;gt; Well, the France is a very sad</text><text start="733.839" dur="4.321">situation. What&amp;#39;s happening in France?</text><text start="736.399" dur="5.201">Because what&amp;#39;s happening in France has</text><text start="738.16" dur="6.799">to do with immigration, not schools, not</text><text start="741.6" dur="5.44">anything. It&amp;#39;s immigration. And I told</text><text start="744.959" dur="3.921">President Mcronone, &amp;quot;Close up your</text><text start="747.04" dur="4.4">borders.&amp;quot; I told him the first time I</text><text start="748.88" dur="4.72">met him, which was years ago in my first</text><text start="751.44" dur="3.76">term, &amp;quot;Close up your borders. You&amp;#39;re</text><text start="753.6" dur="4">going to have nothing but trouble.&amp;quot; And</text><text start="755.2" dur="4.079">they&amp;#39;ve got a lot of trouble. They let</text><text start="757.6" dur="3.12">people into their country that don&amp;#39;t</text><text start="759.279" dur="3.36">love their country. They don&amp;#39;t love</text><text start="760.72" dur="4.64">their buildings. They don&amp;#39;t love their</text><text start="762.639" dur="5.361">art. 